  "pattern": "mutable-state",
  "difficulty_rating": 1425,
  "explanation": "The memo cache is never invalidated or updated for an order id that has already been billed. When order 101 is billed again with a different amount (8), the totals.has(101) guard returns the stale cached 10 instead of recomputing 16, so both calls and the stored value print 10.",
  "prompt": "This memoizes a billed amount per order id, once. Step through both calls for the same order and predict what the second call prints.",
  "language": "javascript",
  "snippet": "const totals = new Map();\nfunction billed(orderId, amount) {\n  if (totals.has(orderId)) return totals.get(orderId);\n  const newTotal = amount * 2;\n  totals.set(orderId, newTotal);\n  return newTotal;\n}\nconsole.log(\"billed:\", billed(101, 5));\nconsole.log(\"billed:\", billed(101, 8));\nconsole.log(\"stored:\", totals.get(101));",
